{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-29T02:15:08.111Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"ccf05b19969ed61664340129","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-29T02:15:08.111Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Portable import review confirms the remaining native read-to-write gap: the installed public update options have no expectedItemHash precondition (upstream 1576), and commitWorkspaceTransaction serializes transactions without excluding ordinary SDK/CLI writes (upstream 1620, verified on SDK 2026.10.25 and 2026.10.28). Future adoption must replace best-effort final hash/history rereads with the public native precondition when available. Existing receipt-payload reader/abandon/replan and scoped staged-document preview needs remain tracked by upstream 1597/1598. Current compensation cancels creations, preserves incoming/outgoing references, checks the real SDK proposal for unowned field side effects, and restores only still-owned field values; it does not claim native-writer isolation. Evidence and reverts remain on pm-memory-1363 and PR 15."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-29T02:15:08.111Z"}],"before_hash":"e4655560733515d4b979436afed917d0490ac84031db06cc231523259619905b","after_hash":"e3a552370296a8ef45942dac97b33913457e701a503dec1db9efa6e688c1a84f","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record